From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:00:53 +0800
Subject: Screencast: do not exclude the Plasma Mobile shell when it is the
 recorder

Plasma Mobile records from its own shell process; excluding the recorder's PID also removed the
wallpaper, launcher and panels (a black home screen). Per-window excludeFromCapture still applies.
Currently gated on MOTO_KWIN_FLAT_OUTPUT; an upstream version would key on the shell, not the host.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Pending
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:recording.quicksetting
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/46
---
 src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
index d30c913..a4b6101 100644
--- a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastmanager.cpp
@@ -103,7 +103,13 @@ void ScreencastManager::streamWaylandOutput(ScreencastStreamV1Interface *wayland
 
 static std::optional<pid_t> getPid(ScreencastStreamV1Interface *waylandStream)
 {
-    if (waylandStream->connection()->executablePath().contains("xdg-desktop-portal-kde")) {
+    const auto executable = waylandStream->connection()->executablePath();
+    // Plasma Mobile records from its own shell process. Excluding that PID
+    // also removes the wallpaper, launcher and panels, yielding a black home
+    // screen. Keep explicit per-window excludeFromCapture filtering intact.
+    const bool mobileShellRecorder = qEnvironmentVariableIsSet("MOTO_KWIN_FLAT_OUTPUT")
+        && executable == QStringLiteral("/usr/bin/plasmashell");
+    if (mobileShellRecorder || executable.contains("xdg-desktop-portal-kde")) {
         // HACK to avoid the portal's windows being hidden
         return std::nullopt;
     }
